  "stplk.w.v.zero": "No locker pays off for any coalition, not even fractionally: every value is 0, and the only core allocation gives every carrier 0.",
  "stplk.w.v.th1": "<b>Zero integrality gap, so Theorem 1 applies:</b> opt(LLP<sub><i>N</i></sub>) = opt(RLLP<sub><i>N</i></sub>) = {v}. Every optimal dual (<i>α</i>, <i>β</i>) of the grand coalition gives a core allocation <i>u<sub>i</sub></i> = Σ<sub><i>k</i>∈<i>C<sub>i</sub></i></sub> <i>β<sub>k</sub></i>; the solver's dual gives <i>u</i> = {u}.",
  "stplk.w.v.tree": "The induced graph is a tree, so the zero gap was guaranteed in advance (Proposition 1, Corollary 2).",
  "stplk.w.v.tu": "The connection matrix is totally unimodular, so the zero gap was guaranteed in advance (Lemma 4, Corollary 1).",
  "stplk.w.v.owners": "The gap depends only on the customers and the locations, not on who owns which customer: tap the customers as you like, and the core stays non-empty.",
  "stplk.w.v.notnec": "<b>The core is non-empty although the gap is positive</b> (opt(RLLP<sub><i>N</i></sub>) = {r} &gt; {v} = opt(LLP<sub><i>N</i></sub>)): Theorem 1 does not apply, and its condition is sufficient, not necessary (Example 6).",
  "stplk.w.v.dual.some": "Scaled by {s}, some optimal dual still gives a core allocation.",
  "stplk.w.v.dual.none": "Scaled by {s}, no optimal dual gives a core allocation: the scaled dual rule misses the core here, whichever dual a solver returns.",
  "stplk.w.v.empty": "<b>The core is empty.</b> To give every coalition what it earns on its own, the carriers would need {need} in total, more than <i>v</i>(<i>N</i>) = {v}. The dual of the LP proves it with weights {w}: the weighted claims of these coalitions already exceed <i>v</i>(<i>N</i>). A subsidy of <i>γ</i> = {g} ({pct} of <i>v</i>(<i>N</i>)) makes the collaboration stable.",
  "stplk.w.v.bound": "The unscaled dual allocation meets every coalition and hands out opt(RLLP<sub><i>N</i></sub>) = {r}, so a subsidy equal to the gap, {gap}, always suffices (a consequence of the proof of Theorem 1 that the article does not state).",
